adigm": "P1_ashby", "claim": "The BLIND advantage is not an artifact of assuming a BLIND report always fixes the blind spot. It survives a hostile parameterisation where BLIND only leads to a structural fix 20% of the time.", "stats": {"n": 8, "treat_mean": 73.125, "ctrl_mean": 315.375, "treat_sd": 120.029, "ctrl_sd": 120.116, "effect": -0.7681, "ci_low": -0.9901, "ci_high": -0.4548}}, {"hid": "H2", "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE", "why": "95% CI [-0.312, 0.466] spans zero -- no reliable effect.", "paradigm": "P1_ashby", "claim": "More sensors, reconciled, does NOT help when blind spots are correlated -- the queued sensor-agree.sh remedy addresses the wrong invariant.", "stats": {"n": 8, "treat_mean": 315.375, "ctrl_mean": 315.375, "treat_sd": 120.116, "ctrl_sd": 120.116, "effect": 0.0, "ci_low": -0.3116, "ci_high": 0.4659}}, {"hid": "H3", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "why": "effect 1.000 >= min_effect 0.1, CI [0.487,1.767].", "paradigm": "P2_perrow", "claim": "Perrow's corollary -- that adding safety devices to an interactively complex, tightly coupled system makes it worse -- DOES transfer to this ecosystem, contradicting bibliothecaire's normal-accidents brief, which argues it does not because the guards sit outside the control path.", "stats": {"n": 8, "treat_mean": 0.552, "ctrl_mean": 0.276, "treat_sd": 0.082, "ctrl_sd": 0.123, "effect": 1.0005, "ci_low": 0.4868, "ci_high": 1.7673}}, {"hid": "H4", "verdict": "FALSIFIED", "why": "effect -0.601 < min_effect 0.1 (CI [0.215,1.195]) -- the falsifier fired.", "paradigm": "P2_perrow", "claim": "Perrow's actual prescription is a COUPLING intervention, not a complexity one: insert slack. Loosening coupling should beat instrumenting, using no new sensors at all.", "stats": {"n": 8, "treat_mean": 504.75, "ctrl_mean": 315.375, "treat_sd": 98.853, "ctrl_sd": 120.116, "effect": 0.6005, "ci_low": 0.2152, "ci_high": 1.1953}}, {"hid": "H5", "verdict": "FALSIFIED", "why": "effect -6.759 < min_effect 0.1 (CI [1.978,95.375]) -- the falsifier fired.", "paradigm": "P3_hayek", "claim": "Hayek's structural claim -- the centre is missing an input that cannot be sent to it -- means NO improvement to central sensing can be the primary remedy. Local self-repair by the organ that holds circumstance-of-time-and-place knowledge should beat the best central-sensing arm.", "stats": {"n": 8, "treat_mean": 84.375, "ctrl_mean": 10.875, "treat_sd": 49.754, "ctrl_sd": 19.114, "effect": 6.7586, "ci_low": 1.9781, "ci_high": 95.375}}, {"hid": "H6", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "why": "effect 0.987 >= min_effect 0.05, CI [-1.000,-0.954].", "paradigm": "P3_hayek", "claim": "Decentralisation and null-discrimination are COMPLEMENTS, not substitutes: local repair handles what the centre cannot see, BLIND handles what local organs cannot know is systemic.", "stats": {"n": 8, "treat_mean": 1.125, "ctrl_mean": 84.375, "treat_sd": 2.976, "ctrl_sd": 49.754, "effect": -0.9867, "ci_low": -1.0, "ci_high": -0.9537}}]}